# Copy to meta_secrets.properties (gitignored, never commit the real
# token) and fill in the real values, then push to the phone at
# /data/adb/dashboard/meta_secrets.properties.
#
# Optional - if this file is missing, akd_followers_fetch.sh falls back
# to sourcing Instagram/Facebook numbers from AKD's own API like
# before. Set this up to bypass AKD for those two platforms entirely
# and hit the Meta Graph API directly, so a stale/expired token on
# AKD's side (a real recurring issue, first hit 2026-07-04) stops being
# a single point of failure for the router dashboard's own display of
# these numbers.
#
# How to get each value (all done in your own browser, logged into the
# Facebook account that manages the Instagram Business/Creator account
# and the Facebook Page - this can't be done on your behalf, Meta
# requires it be generated interactively by the account owner):
#
# 1. Go to https://developers.facebook.com/tools/explorer/
# 2. Select your app (or create one - Meta requires an app to issue
#    tokens even for read-only access to your own pages, no App Review
#    needed for reading your own Page's/IG account's public-ish fields).
# 3. Click "Get Token" > "Get User Access Token", grant these
#    permissions: pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement,
#    instagram_basic.
# 4. Under "Get Token" again, switch to "Get Page Access Token" for
#    your specific Page - this is the token to use below (Page tokens
#    for your own Page don't expire the way User tokens do, as long as
#    the User token they were derived from was itself long-lived - use
#    the Access Token Debugger, https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug/accesstoken/,
#    to confirm "Expires: Never" before using it here).
# 5. META_FB_PAGE_ID: shown in that same Page Access Token dropdown, or
#    on the Page's own "About" page under Facebook.
# 6. META_IG_USER_ID: with the Page Access Token from step 4, query
#    https://graph.facebook.com/v19.0/<PAGE_ID>?fields=instagram_business_account&access_token=<TOKEN>
#    in the Graph API Explorer - the returned instagram_business_account.id
#    is this value (only works if the Instagram account is a
#    Business/Creator account linked to that Facebook Page).

META_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_long_lived_page_access_token_here
META_FB_PAGE_ID=your_facebook_page_id_here
META_IG_USER_ID=your_instagram_business_account_id_here
